" A Useful Example
:imap <TAB> <C-N>
" above mapping becomes annoying with collisions (cases where the 
"		mapping doesnt do want we want)
"	we do NOT want completion when there is a blank line, and there
"		we just want an indent

" How can we make this DUMB mapping SMART?
" Define the specific behavior: Only completion when the cursor is
" in front of a partial word

" we <TAB> to do both: indentation and completion

function! TabOrCompletion()
	let col = col('.')-1
	if col==0 || getline('.')[col-1] !~ '\k'
		return "\<TAB>"
	else
		return "\<C-N>"
	endif
endfunction

:inoremap <expr> <TAB> TabOrCompletion()

" col('.') get the column number of the cursor
			" 'need to work out the context around the cursor'
			" *vim starts counting columns at 1
			" the offset of 1 is b/c we will use this variable to index the line
			"		which is a string and indexing starts a 0
