" Debugging
" :h debug-script

" to enter the interactive debugger
:debug call Myfunc()

" to debug .vimrc or plugins or syntax files, start Vim with -D flag
$ vi -D somefile
 
" In the debugger mode you get a  > prompt

debugger commands:
	cont continue
		run til next breakpoint
	step
		execute next script command (stepping into fx calls)
	next 
		same as step but steps over functions calls
	interupt
		simulate a 'control c'
	quit
		abort entire script

Adding BreakPoints - from with in the interactive debugger
	syntax:		breakadd <func|file> <line_num> <file path|func name>

example breakpoint adding

	breakadd func MyFunc	" break at the start of function named MyFunc
	breakdd func 10 MyFunc	" break at 10th line relative to start of MyFunc

	breakadd file 	~/.vimrc  " break at start of script of file
	breakadd file 42 ~/.vimrc  " break at absolute line number in file

	breakadd here 	" set break point at current line of current file
			** be careful ** NOT at the current line in the interactive 
							 debugging processes 
	breaklist		" list all current breakpoints

	breakdel func MyFunc	" delete break at the start of function named MyFunc
	breakdel func 10 MyFunc	" delete break at 10th line relative to start of MyFunc

	breakdel file 	~/.vimrc  " delete break at start of script of file
	breakdel file 42 ~/.vimrc  " delete break at absolute line number in file

	breakdel * 		delete all break points
	breakdel 7		delete the 7th breakpoiint as numbered in the breaklist
